  "id": "DrugBank_DB01188 - MONDO_5982",
  "verbalization": "Ciclopirox, a topical antifungal agent, is linked to Tinea Infection through a chain of indications that involve related fungal infections. The evidence suggests that Ciclopirox is used to treat Tinea Unguium, a fungal infection of the nails, which in turn is associated with Tinea Infection, a broader fungal infection affecting the skin. Similarly, Ciclopirox is also indicated for Pityriasis Versicolor, another fungal infection, which is linked to Tinea Infection. This indicates that Ciclopirox may exert antifungal effects through a common mechanism, possibly targeting fungal cell membranes or inhibiting fungal growth. The overlapping indications suggest that Ciclopirox may be effective against a range of fungal infections, potentially due to shared biochemical pathways or mechanisms of action. The evidence supports a relationship between Ciclopirox and Tinea Infection through a chain of indications, highlighting the role of antifungal agents in treating diverse fungal infections.",
